export default "# Kevro Apps (the studio)\n\nKevro Apps is a small independent software studio in Doha, Qatar. It makes calm, family-friendly Islamic apps for Android. There are three apps: Islamic Coloring for Kids (on Google Play), Qur'aan Class (in closed testing on Google Play) and Ayah Play (coming to Google Play).\n\nContact: support@kevroapps.com. Replies come within one business day. The contact page is https://kevroapps.com/contact/.\n\nAll apps: Android only. For questions about iPhone, the assistant offers the support email. No ads. No tracking. No data is sold. Every app has its own privacy policy:\n- Islamic Coloring for Kids: https://kevroapps.com/privacy/\n- Qur'aan Class: https://kevroapps.com/quraan-class/privacy/ (English and Arabic), and how to delete a Qur'aan Class account: https://kevroapps.com/quraan-class/delete-account/\n- Ayah Play: https://kevroapps.com/ayah-play/privacy/\n\nApps page: https://kevroapps.com/apps/\n\nWebsites: the studio has built websites and automation for small businesses in the past. It is not taking new website clients at the moment.\n\nThe website is in English. There is no Arabic version of the site yet. Qur'aan Class itself works in English and Arabic.\n\nQuestions the assistant cannot answer: prices, release dates, refunds, anything about a specific person's account or order, legal questions. For these it offers to pass the question to the studio by email.\n\nSource: kevro_business/AGENCY.md, site pages on kevroapps.com (4 Nov 2026).\n\n---\n\n# Islamic Coloring for Kids\n\nA calm coloring book and learning app for Muslim kids, on Google Play for Android (phones and tablets, portrait or landscape). Link: https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.islamickids.islamic_coloring . Android only. For questions about iPhone, the assistant offers the support email. Made for young children.\n\nWhat is in it:\n- More than 80 coloring pages: the Kaaba, mosques, nature, fruits and clothing. Fill a shape with one tap or paint with the brush. Six simple tools: fill, brush, eraser, shapes, text and glitter. Free Draw gives a blank page.\n- The Arabic alphabet: all 28 Arabic letters, free, each with a pronunciation the child can tap to hear. Ten Arabic numbers with objects to count. The twelve Islamic months in calligraphy, from Muharram to Dhul Hijjah, including Ramadan.\n- Puzzle Studio: 36 pictures across six worlds, sliding tiles or a classic jigsaw, from 4 pieces up to 36.\n- Works offline once installed.\n\nMoney, stated plainly:\n- No ads of any kind.\n- No subscription. Extra packs are one-time purchases: pay once and keep them. Nothing renews.\n- 42 items are free, including every Arabic letter, the Free Draw canvas, two pages in each of the five art collections, and the first item in every pack.\n- There is a Ramadan offer on at the moment. For the prices, see the Google Play listing. The assistant never quotes a price, a percentage or an end date, and never says what a price \"was\".\n\nSafety for children: no accounts or sign-in, no personal information collected, nothing the child can reach links out of the app. Purchases, settings and sharing sit behind a grown-up check, and parents can set their own passcode. Kid Mode pins the app to the screen so small hands cannot wander into other apps. Artwork is saved on the device in My Artwork and a parent can save a picture to the gallery or share it. The illustrations contain no faces or figures.\n\nRefunds and purchase problems go through Google Play, or by email to support@kevroapps.com.\n\nSource: islamic_coloring/docs/store_listing_2026-11.md, AGENCY.md (4 Nov 2026).\n\n---\n\n# Qur'aan Class (Arabic name: حلقة القرآن)\n\nAn Android app for teachers who run a Qur'aan or Arabic class, and for the students and families who learn with them. It is in closed testing on Google Play. There is no public release date and no price to quote. Android only. For questions about iPhone, the assistant offers the support email. The whole app works in English and Arabic, and each person chooses their own language.\n\nHow it works: the teacher sets homework, keeps the memorisation record and marks the register. Students see what is due and send their recitations. Parents follow along and talk with the teacher. Homework, records and messages stay in one place.\n\nFor teachers: set homework by surah and ayah, juz, page, or in their own words; keep a daily memorisation record (new memorisation, recent revision, older revision); see what is due for revision; listen to recorded recitations and accept them or ask for another go; record how a portion should sound; take the register (present, late, absent or excused); write to one family or send one announcement to the whole class; run a recitation competition; give certificates and stars; share a monthly or term progress report as a PDF; keep a simple record of fees families have paid; lessons show in each family's own time zone with the teacher's lesson link.\n\nFor students: see homework on a calendar, record a recitation and send it to the teacher, collect stickers, stars and certificates in a learning journal.\n\nFor parents: follow the child's homework, memorisation record and attendance; hear accepted recitations and the teacher's own recitation; tell the teacher in advance when the child will be away; message the teacher in the child's group.\n\nPrivacy: students and parents join with a code from their teacher, so no email is needed for them. Recordings are kept for a set time, then removed. A student never sees fees or a parent's contact details. No ads and no tracking. A child under 16 can record only once a parent has turned recordings on. The assistant never asks for a child's name or details. Policy: https://kevroapps.com/quraan-class/privacy/ . Deleting an account: https://kevroapps.com/quraan-class/delete-account/ .\n\nTesting: Qur'aan Class is in a closed test. People who want to help test can email support@kevroapps.com from the Gmail on their Android phone; the page https://kevroapps.com/tester/ explains the steps. The assistant says nothing about test dates or numbers.\n\nSource: quran_homework/docs/play_store/listing.md, kevroapps.com/tester/ (4 Nov 2026).\n\n---\n\n# Ayah Play\n\nA calm Qur'aan app for the youngest children, around ages two to five. A short surah plays while the child taps a few gentle toys on the screen. There is no internet access, no ads and no account, and the settings sit behind a parent gate. It is coming to Google Play. There is no release date and the assistant does not guess one. Android only.\n\nIts privacy policy is live: https://kevroapps.com/ayah-play/privacy/ . The assistant says nothing more about Ayah Play than this file. For anything else it offers the support email.\n\nSource: kevroapps.com/apps/ and /ayah-play/privacy/ (4 Nov 2026), AGENCY.md (\"coming to Google Play; nothing more\").";
